The Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3 is a **WiFi-only** board — no ethernet PHY. ESPHome's transport selector in MajiFlow is locked on WiFi.

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Default for this board | WiFi (forced) |
| Credentials needed | SSID + password |
| Diagnostic sensors | `wifi_info` (IP, SSID, MAC) + `wifi_signal` (dBm) |
| Static IP support | ✓ via *Connection → IP Configuration* |
| Fallback when network is down | SoftAP starts automatically |

### Recovery path

When the configured WiFi network is unreachable, ESPHome activates a fallback hotspot after **~90 seconds** of failed station association ([`wifi.ap_timeout`](https://esphome.io/components/wifi.html) default). MajiFlow does not currently override this — if you need faster recovery during commissioning, edit the generated YAML to add `wifi.ap_timeout: 30s` before flashing.

- **SoftAP SSID**: `<friendly_name> Fallback` — the device's friendly name from MajiFlow.
- **SoftAP password**: identical to your `wifi_password` — one credential to remember.
- **Default gateway**: **`192.168.4.1`** — connect your phone/laptop to the SoftAP first, then the OS pops the captive-portal page automatically. Use it to **re-enter WiFi credentials** (`/wifisave`) or **push an OTA firmware update** (`/update`). Typing `http://192.168.4.1/` directly may land on the entity dashboard instead of the wifi-recovery page (known ESPHome ordering quirk — [#11132](https://github.com/esphome/esphome/issues/11132), [#14856](https://github.com/esphome/esphome/issues/14856)); the captive-portal *routes* still work, just navigate via the OS popup.

### Web dashboard

Emitted on **port 80**. Reachable at:

- `http://<device-ip>/` on the home network — IP shown in `wifi_info`.
- `http://192.168.4.1/` on the fallback AP — but entity controls won't function without STA (no time, no API). Use the captive-portal popup for credential reset; return to the home-network IP once the device reconnects.

Every relay, sensor, switch, and number entity declared in the topology is exposed for manual control.

### Range note

The Heltec's WiFi antenna is the chip antenna on the board edge. For installations behind metal enclosures or far from the access point, plan a WiFi repeater or use the LoRa transport instead (entity-level — not the ESPHome network transport).
